From: ReiKatari <reikatari@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0008] freedreno/vulkan: Double-buffered ping-pong command submission with timeline semaphores

Implements zero-stall CPU command submission by recording alternating ping-pong
command buffers A and B, eliminating CPU stall bubbles while GPU executes prior
draw workloads.

---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.c b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.c
index e492c10..f981bc2 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -1205,6 +1205,26 @@ tu_submit_ping_pong(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd)
 {
+   /* Alternate between ring buffer chunks A and B */
+   uint32_t active_idx = cmd->ping_pong_index;
+   cmd->ping_pong_index ^= 1;
+   
+   /* Signal completion via timeline semaphore without blocking CPU thread */
+   struct tu_queue *queue = cmd->device->queues[0];
+   tu_queue_submit_async(queue, cmd->ping_pong_buffers[active_idx], cmd->timeline_semaphore, ++cmd->timeline_value);
 }
